<Layout title="Broker Reviews" description="Our broker review methodology, and how to evaluate any forex broker yourself while our hands-on reviews are in progress.">
  <h1>Broker Reviews</h1>
  <p>We haven't published individual broker reviews yet — and we'd rather tell you why than fill this page with numbers we haven't checked.</p>

  <h2>Why this page is empty (on purpose)</h2>
  <p>Most "best forex broker" pages you'll find are ranked by affiliate commission, and the spreads and withdrawal times quoted on them are copied from the broker's own marketing rather than measured. Those numbers go stale fast, and a wrong number here could cost you real money.</p>
  <p>Our policy is that we don't publish a broker-specific figure — spread, commission, swap rate, withdrawal processing time — until we've opened an account and tested it ourselves. That testing is in progress. Until it's done, this page stays honest rather than full.</p>

  <h2>What our reviews will actually cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Licence verification</strong> — which specific legal entity holds your account as a Philippine resident, and confirmation of that entity on the regulator's own register.</li>
    <li><strong>Real cost of trading</strong> — measured spreads on the pairs people actually trade, plus commission and overnight swap, not just the advertised headline number.</li>
    <li><strong>Deposit and withdrawal, tested end to end</strong> — including how long a withdrawal actually took, since this is the single most common source of broker complaints.</li>
    <li><strong>Account protections</strong> — whether negative balance protection and segregated client funds apply to the entity you'd be contracting with.</li>
    <li><strong>Platform and support</strong> — what the experience is actually like, tested rather than described.</li>
  </ul>

